<title>USA: Ohio unemployment rate down 0.8 percent in March.</title>
<headline>Ohio unemployment rate down 0.8 percent in March.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The seasonally adjusted unemployment rate for Ohio dropped to 4.7 percent in March from 5.5 percent the previous month, the Ohio Bureau of Employment Services reported Friday.</p>
<p>The rate for February was &quot;unrealistically high&quot; and the March figures more accurately reflect the Ohio labor market, according to the bureau.</p>
<p>The number of Ohio residents with jobs rose 12,000 in March to nearly 5.5 million, the bureau reported. The March 1996 unemployment rate was 5 percent, the bureau noted.</p>
<p>((--David Bailey, 312-408-8647))</p>
